          "code": "GENERATE_TEAMS_POST_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1768597086532",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768597086535_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to generate content for an internal or external post to Microsoft teams or Slacks Channel by following these guidelines:\n\nYou are provided with one or both of the following input parameters:\npromptInstructions ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptInstructions}} ) : This indicates instructions for composing a post, which may be empty or null\npreviousCommunicationText ( {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.previousCommunicationText}} ) : Text excerpted from a previous communication (such as an SMS or Email), which may be empty or null\n\nIf {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptInstructions}} is provided and not empty, use this as the primary basis for creating both a concise, informative subject and message body.\nIf {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.previousCommunicationText}} is provided and not empty, analyze previousCommunicationText and derive a suitable subject and message body reflecting the intent and main points of the original text.\n\nEnsure the tone is professional, clear, and appropriate for a business audience. This will be used to send the message to Microsoft teams channel or Slacks channel, please add some basic html tags and stylings which are supported by both slack api and microsoft teams bot framework.\n\nThe response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language.\n\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON array with objects containing only \"subject\" and \"body\" fields. Your entire response/output is going to consist of a single JSON object {}, and do NOT wrap it within JSON md markers. As in the example below:\n{\"subject\":\"Let's Make a difference Together ! Volunteer with IDC Hyderabad\",\n\"body\":\"Join us in making a positive impact within our community! IDC Hyderabad is organizing a series of volunteer initiatives and we invite you to be a part of these meaningful activities. Whether it's supporting local causes, participating in community outreach, or lending a helping hand to those in need, your involvement can make a significant difference.Volunteering is a rewarding opportunity to develop new skills, build relationships with colleagues, and contribute to social good. We encourage everyone to participate, no matter your level of experience or availability.If you're interested in participating or would like more information about upcoming volunteer events, please reply to this message or reach out to our team directly.Let's work together to create a positive change—your support matters!\"}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"body\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
